/.nb-gradle/

# Top-level build/ is a real Maven module directory (build/gcm-md-parent/, the parent POM every
# other module in this reactor inherits from), not a build-output dir - it must never be
# blanket-ignored. This used to be a bare `build/` pattern (matches "build" at any depth,
# including the repo root) with a `!/build/gcm-md-parent/` negation meant to carve out an
# exception - which never worked: git will not re-include a path whose parent directory is
# already excluded, no matter how the negation is written, and `build/` excludes /build/ itself.
# Confirmed the hard way: a fresh checkout (gitlab-ci-local, simulating a real CI runner) failed
# every single job with "Non-resolvable parent POM" because build/gcm-md-parent/pom.xml was
# never actually tracked by git at all. Anchored + one-level (leading /, trailing /*) so this
# only affects direct children of the top-level build/, not any nested build/ dir elsewhere in
# the tree (still caught by the recursive pattern below, which - unlike the old one - correctly
# excludes the top-level path since it requires at least one path segment before "build/").
/build/*
!/build/gcm-md-parent/
**/*/build/
!**/src/main/**/build/
!**/src/test/**/build/

